      "body": "Stack from [ghstack](https://github.com/ezyang/ghstack/tree/0.15.0) (oldest at bottom):\n* __->__ #5418\n\nFixes #5362.\n\n## Agent details\n\nPrepared with Codex. The fixture change and local testing limitations were reviewed with the author.\n\n### Summary\n\nThe precompile bitwise fixture omitted `training`. After #5023, `compile_time_passes()` reads `config.training.disable_cuda_graphs`, so both Llama3 and Qwen3 MoE precompile comparisons fail before saving their artifacts.\n\nReuse `build_minimal_trainer()` to obtain the same configuration and loss function as the direct-trace comparison. Its existing `TrainingConfig(disable_cuda_graphs=True)` keeps both paths configured consistently. Pass the shared single-device parallelism context when constructing the compile-time passes.\n\n### Test Plan\n\n- Reproduced the exact missing-`training` AttributeError before the fix.\n- Both affected precompile tests passed with fresh Inductor caches and FX graph caching disabled. Their existing assertions verify bitwise-identical loss, parameter hashes, and gradient hashes after five optimizer steps with seed 42 and deterministic algorithms enabled.\n- All 27 precompile unit tests passed, including standalone Inductor artifact save/load and explicitly enabled CUDA-graph annotation selection.\n- Changed-file pre-commit hooks and `git diff --check` passed. The project type checker excludes tests.\n\n```bash\npython -m pytest -p force_fa2 \\\n  torchtitan/experiments/graph_trainer/tests/test_bitwise_deterministic.py::TestLlama3BitwiseDeterministic::test_precompile_vs_trace \\\n  torchtitan/experiments/graph_trainer/tests/test_bitwise_deterministic.py::TestQwen3MoEBitwiseDeterministic::test_precompile_vs_trace \\\n  -v --tb=short\npython -m pytest torchtitan/experiments/graph_trainer/tests/test_precompile.py -v --tb=short\nSKIP=pyrefly-check pre-commit run --files torchtitan/experiments/graph_trainer/tests/test_bitwise_deterministic.py\npre-commit run --all-files\ngit diff --check\n```\n\nLocal GPU validation used H100 with PyTorch's built-in FA2 to match A10G CI. A temporary pytest plugin, outside the repository, makes `get_cuda_flash_attention_impl()` return `None`; FA3 was unavailable locally.\n\nFull-repository pre-commit did not pass: cached Python 3.9 hooks cannot parse existing `match` statements, and Pyrefly reports unrelated errors outside the changed file, including missing optional imports. These limitations are recorded for this draft PR.",
